Add notes, roadmap, FAQ, articles, and policy pages (3.1.0)

Home page:
- What's New, built from the latest CHANGELOG.MD entry
- Roadmap (in progress / planned / shipped), edited in content.go
- Articles: latest Medium posts, fetched at build time; falls back to a
  link if Medium is unreachable, never fails the build
- FAQ, edited in content.go
- "Last checked" time under the upstream status list

Engineering Notes: Markdown files in notes/ are published under /notes/ on
each build. Optional front matter (description, tags, dates); dates
otherwise come from git history, so the deploy now checks out full history.
Each note gets a table of contents, copy buttons on code blocks, linkable
headings, related notes by shared tag, a byline and author box crediting
covertdaemon (Cloud Engineer), and TechArticle structured data. The index has live
search and tag filtering; each tag has its own page; /notes/feed.xml is an
RSS feed. Every note is scanned for credential-like strings and the build
fails on a match. First note: building a static site with Hugo, with a
Lessons Learned section.

Adds a 1200x630 link-preview image built from the Q brand mark.

Adds unit tests (go test ./..., make test), run in the deploy workflow.

New pages: /security.html, /accessibility.html, /terms-of-use.html, and a
custom 404.html. Changelog links point to CHANGELOG.MD on GitHub.

Generated on every build: sitemap.xml, robots.txt, and
/.well-known/security.txt (RFC 9116, Expires one year out).

Every templated page gets canonical, Open Graph and Twitter card tags.
The footer links to every policy page and shows version and build date.
Sidebar links are root-relative so they work from secondary pages.
Optional Cloudflare Web Analytics, emitted only when a token is set.

Everything runs at build time; the output is still plain static files on
GitHub Pages. Adds github.com/yuin/goldmark for Markdown rendering.

Trims the 2.0.0 and 3.0.0 changelog entries down to what changed, and
removes the README section on the old protected area.

